@loveandbeepbrother/dsh-tts-service README · dsh-tts-service：There is **no default provider and no default voice**. Until you pick one, `tts_service_say` fails with
`VOICE_NOT_SELECTED` and tells the agent where to pick it.

This version synthesizes whole clips (no streaming).

@loveandbeepbrother/dsh-tts-service README · Alibaba Bailian (`tts-bailian`, provider id `bailian`)：- CosyVoice and Qwen-Audio-TTS use `/api/v1/services/audio/tts/SpeechSynthesizer`; Qwen3-TTS uses
  `/api/v1/services/aigc/multimodal-generation/generation`. Both return a 24-hour audio URL, which the plugin downloads.
- Tone descriptions (`instruction`), per the official docs:

@loveandbeepbrother/dsh-tts-service README · `tts_service_voices`：Lists the current selection and, per provider, its voices. Optional parameters: `provider`, `language`, `search`
(substring of id, name or description) and `refresh`. At most 60 voices per provider are shown. Pressing stop ends it
right away, even while a provider is still answering.

@loveandbeepbrother/dsh-tts-service README · Outputs：`speaker-windows` counts as available when there was keyboard or mouse input in the last `presentMinutes` (default 5)
and the screen is not locked (Windows PowerShell: `GetLastInputInfo`, `LogonUI.exe`). Playback uses
`System.Media.SoundPlayer`, one clip at a time; the tool does not wait for it to finish.

